<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hosokawa Harumoto</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1514">1514</a>–<a href="/years/1563">1563</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hosokawa Harumoto was a Japanese warlord who served as kanrei, deputy to the Ashikaga <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogun</a>, and dominated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyoto">Kyoto</a> in the 1530s and 1540s. His power rested on his retainers, above all the Miyoshi, but in 1549 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miyoshi-nagayoshi">Miyoshi Nagayoshi</a> turned against him and defeated his forces at Eguchi, forcing him and the shogun to flee the capital. He lost his authority and died in confinement, marking the eclipse of the Hosokawa family.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hosokawa-harumoto.jpg" alt="Hosokawa Harumoto" width="186" height="273" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 所司代 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E7%B4%B0%E5%B7%9D%E5%8F%B3%E4%BA%AC%E5%A4%A7%E5%A4%AB%E6%99%B4%E5%85%83.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
